1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,845
A: Most pharmacies still run on fax machines, phone calls, paper logs, and systems that don't talk to each other.

2
00:00:05,845 --> 00:00:09,845
A: Chimera Rx is one connected ledger, from the dock to the pickup counter.

3
00:00:09,845 --> 00:00:11,998
A: Here is every tab a pharmacist uses.

4
00:00:12,058 --> 00:00:13,567
A: Today is the pharmacist's home.

5
00:00:13,567 --> 00:00:18,698
A: Deliveries to check in, stock to watch, and suggestions from the AI agents, all in one place.

6
00:00:18,758 --> 00:00:20,193
A: Receiving starts at the dock.

7
00:00:20,193 --> 00:00:25,358
A: One scan with the camera reads the lot, serial, and expiry, with no typing and no paper log.

8
00:00:25,418 --> 00:00:29,100
A: Four checks run: the invoice, the paperwork, the expiry, and the recall list.

9
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:31,082
A: Then put-away is recorded, with the bay.

10
00:00:31,142 --> 00:00:34,614
A: Inventory shows every lot on the shelf, by store, with its expiry.

11
00:00:34,614 --> 00:00:40,400
A: Filter for what is expiring, what is refrigerated, and what is controlled, and a count is always one click away.

12
00:00:40,460 --> 00:00:42,353
A: Register handles the sale at the counter.

13
00:00:42,353 --> 00:00:48,031
A: Pick an item, mark it paid, and the receipt prints, with the sale recorded against the same ledger as everything else.

14
00:00:48,091 --> 00:00:54,703
A: Stock help suggests what to reorder and what is close to expiry, so the pharmacy orders what it needs and stops throwing medicine away.

15
00:00:54,763 --> 00:00:56,389
A: Transfers move stock between two stores.

16
00:00:56,389 --> 00:01:02,349
A: Pick a lot, move it, and the transfer lands in both stores' audit logs, with no phone call and no paper slip.

17
00:01:02,409 --> 00:01:04,534
A: Fill and pickup is where it all meets.

18
00:01:04,534 --> 00:01:10,643
A: Rx Guardian reviews an order the moment it arrives, and shows the evidence from the patient's own history, so nothing is a guess.

19
00:01:10,703 --> 00:01:15,711
A: Accept the suggestion, and the order goes on hold with the reason recorded in the audit log.

20
00:01:15,711 --> 00:01:19,246
A: The pharmacist always decides, and the agent never changes an order itself.

21
00:01:19,306 --> 00:01:21,015
A: That is the dock to the counter.

22
00:01:21,015 --> 00:01:22,969
A: Over to my co-host for the care side.

23
00:01:23,029 --> 00:01:24,181
B: Patients holds each history.

24
00:01:24,181 --> 00:01:29,940
B: Search for a patient, state why you are opening the profile, and that reason is written to the audit log.

25
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,953
B: Here is one gap old systems leave.

26
00:01:31,953 --> 00:01:35,301
B: A recall arrives by fax, and nobody knows who got which lot.

27
00:01:35,301 --> 00:01:37,254
B: Connected, the lots are read from it.

28
00:01:37,314 --> 00:01:40,843
B: The pharmacist confirms each lot, and the affected patients appear.

29
00:01:40,903 --> 00:01:43,207
B: Messages are drafted for exactly those patients.

30
00:01:43,207 --> 00:01:47,487
B: The pharmacist attests, and only then do they go out, to the sandbox.

31
00:01:47,547 --> 00:01:52,581
B: Refills lists who is due, drafts reminders, and flags prescriptions that need a new one.

32
00:01:52,641 --> 00:01:58,022
B: DSCSA and trace exports the product history, and checks serials in a sandbox.

33
00:01:58,082 --> 00:02:02,503
B: Every message lands in the sandbox outbox, so nothing reaches a real person.

34
00:02:02,563 --> 00:02:03,877
B: Now the AI agents.

35
00:02:03,877 --> 00:02:05,520
B: Eight work in the background.

36
00:02:05,520 --> 00:02:10,120
B: Rules decide, the model explains, a gate checks the model, and a pharmacist decides.

37
00:02:10,180 --> 00:02:14,337
B: Run Rx Guardian now, and it flags what a busy pharmacist could miss.

38
00:02:14,337 --> 00:02:16,256
B: It never changes an order itself.

39
00:02:16,316 --> 00:02:18,442
B: Pick any provider, even a local model.

40
00:02:18,442 --> 00:02:22,086
B: Patient names stay out of the prompts, and every run is logged.

41
00:02:22,146 --> 00:02:28,503
B: Integrations speak open standards: REST, an MCP server, FHIR behind OAuth, and signed webhooks.

42
00:02:28,563 --> 00:02:33,760
B: Real connections, like text, email and e-prescribing, are designed seams, sandboxed today.

43
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:35,908
B: Roles are enforced on the server.

44
00:02:35,908 --> 00:02:40,085
B: A cashier never sees allergies, and an admin never touches anything clinical.

45
00:02:40,145 --> 00:02:44,017
B: PHI is encrypted and the audit log is hash-chained.

46
00:02:44,017 --> 00:02:45,738
B: HIPAA-style safeguards, not certified.

47
00:02:45,798 --> 00:02:50,742
B: Built with Kiro: specs, steering, hooks, and a Kiro Crew team, with a human at every gate.

48
00:02:50,802 --> 00:02:51,700
B: Chimera Rx.

49
00:02:51,700 --> 00:02:53,495
B: github.com/pjborad/Chimera-Rx.

50
00:02:53,495 --> 00:02:55,291
B: pjborad.github.io/Chimera-Rx.

